1
00:04:41,250 --> 00:04:47,250
The groove is on the move.

2
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:28,500
Kronk's New Groove is a animation, comedy, family
film directed by Saul Blinkoff.

3
00:14:03,750 --> 00:14:09,750
Kronk, now chef and Head Delivery Boy of Mudka's Meat Hut, is
fretting over the upcoming visit of his father.

4
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Kronk's father always disapproved of young Kronk's culinary interests and wished that
Kronk instead would settle down with a wife and a large house on a hill.

5
00:23:26,250 --> 00:23:32,250
Kronk (voice), played by Patrick Warburton.

6
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:13,500
Ms. Birdwell (voice), played by Tracey Ullman.

7
00:32:48,750 --> 00:32:54,750
Yzma (voice), played by Eartha Kitt.

8
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Kuzco (voice), played by David Spade.

9
00:42:11,250 --> 00:42:17,250
Pacha (voice), played by John Goodman.

10
00:46:52,500 --> 00:46:58,500
Chicha (voice), played by Wendie Malick.

11
00:51:33,750 --> 00:51:39,750
Kronk's New Groove (also known as The Emperor's New Groove 2: Kronk's New Groove) is a 2005 American animated direct-to-video
musical comedy film animated by Toon City Animation and released by Walt Disney Home Entertainment on December 13, 2005.

12
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
The film is the sequel to The Emperor's New Groove (2000), with David Spade, John Goodman, Eartha Kitt, Patrick Warburton
and Wendie Malick returning from the first film, and John Mahoney and Tracey Ullman voicing new characters.

13
01:00:56,250 --> 01:01:02,250
It was also the last film to feature the voice of John
Fiedler, who died six months before it was released.

14
01:05:37,500 --> 01:05:43,500
The film explores themes of friendship, competition, sequel, hilarious.

15
01:10:18,750 --> 01:10:24,750
The tone is lighthearted.
